body:
[`[HTMLConstructor]`][1] defines [overrriden construction steps][2]. If I’m interpreting them correctly, the following script should throw a TypeError ([step 3][3]). Firefox exhibits the behavior I expected, but in Chrome and Safari, it looks like `Get(NewTarget, "prototype")` ([step 8][4]) happens prior to step 3:

```js
const newTarget = Object.defineProperty(function() {}.bind(), 'prototype', {
  get() {
    throw new Error('Get(NewTarget, "prototype")');
  }
});

Reflect.construct(HTMLElement, [], newTarget);

// Chrome: 
// Uncaught Error: Get(NewTarget, "prototype")

// Firefox:
// TypeError: Illegal constructor.

// Safari:
// Error: Get(NewTarget, "prototype")
```

I think the following script is also specced to throw ([step 5][5]) before the property access, but in this case, Chrome, Firefox, and Safari all agree on evaluating `new.target.prototype` first:

```js
const newTarget = Object.defineProperty(function() {}.bind(), 'prototype', {
  get() {
    throw new Error('Get(NewTarget, "prototype")');
  }
});

customElements.define('x-x', newTarget);

Reflect.construct(HTMLAnchorElement, [], newTarget);

// Chrome:
// Uncaught Error: Get(NewTarget, "prototype")

// Firefox:
// Error: Get(NewTarget, "prototype")

// Safari:
// Error: Get(NewTarget, "prototype")
```

What behaviors are correct in these two cases?

If I’m correct that the second example is currently specced to throw before the property access, should the ordering of the steps be changed to match web reality, given three major browsers already do the same thing?

---

Edit: previously included incorrect note about FF/Chrome not honoring step 9. The issue was in the test code.

[1]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#htmlconstructor
[2]: https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#overridden-constructor-steps
[3]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#html-element-constructors:concept-custom-element-definition-constructor
[4]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#html-element-constructors:newtarget-6
[5]: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#html-element-constructors:concept-custom-element-definition-local-name
